messages:
alex: Pasting a few screenshots of the dashboard on a narrow phone — main issue: table columns overflow and the left sidebar covers content when we collapse it. Thoughts on breakpoints?

rachel: thanks for the screenshots. do we have a prototype? my quick thought: hide non-essential columns under ~720px and show a row details drawer. avoid horizontal scroll if possible.

samir: +1 to the drawer idea. also we should not overlay the sidebar as a permanent overlay on mobile — convert it to a temporary slide-over with an explicit close button and focus trap.

jamie: agree. quick accessibility nit: when the sidebar opens on mobile, focus should move to the first item and there should be an aria-label on the close icon. a11y-bot: contrast check failed for the sidebar muted header (2.8:1).

alex: good call. rachel — can we prioritize which columns are essential? my initial list: name, model, status, last run. everything else can go into the row details drawer.

rachel: yep. i can mock a collapsing column strategy: at widths < 900px collapse 'tags' and 'region', < 720px collapse 'model' into abbreviated text with a tooltip, < 480px show only name + status and the chevron for details.

matt: for the table overflow, we can also experiment with cell text truncation + tooltip rather than forcing scroll. small screens should allow multi-line cells for description fields. also consider making the table full-bleed when the sidebar is hidden.

samir: CSS idea (for prototype):
```css
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .dashboard-table td.model, .dashboard-table td.region { display: none; }
  .dashboard-table td.name { white-space: normal; }
}
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .dashboard-table td.status { order: 2; }
  .dashboard-table .row-actions { position: absolute; right: 12px; }
}
```

jamie: looks reasonable. just ensure touch targets remain >= 44px.

alex: copy tweak: instead of the button text 'View details' can we use 'Open details' for consistency with other slide-over actions? also prefer 'Model version' vs 'Model' in the table header.

rachel: noted. i'll update the mockups and push a new Figma page. i'll add a second mock showing the sidebar as a slide-over with a backdrop that traps focus.

a11y-bot: reminder: when converting columns to an accordion/drawer, ensure each expanded panel has aria-expanded and the drawer has role="dialog" + aria-modal="true".

matt: performance note — if we hide columns, don't re-render huge tables on breakpoint change; debounce and virtualize rows where possible.

alex: action items: rachel to produce 3 mocks (desktop, tablet, mobile), jamie to write a short a11y checklist for the slide-over and table, samir to prototype slide-over behavior, matt to check table virtualization impact. i'll run a 5-user phone usability run once mocks are in. emoji :rocket:

rachel: filing this as a short design ticket now, will ping when Figma link is ready.

samir: also adding a quick CSS accessibility test to CI for focus outline visibility when sidebar opens.

jamie: thanks all, looks like a clear path forward. :thumbsup:
